schema_version: '1.0'
decision:
  action: improve
  weakness_id: W-BOUNDARY-CROSS-GAP
  failure_class: coverage_gap
  failure_mechanism: missing_boundary_bins
  source: mixed
  confidence: high
diagnosis:
  observed_problem: "The boundary_data_concurrent covercross bin (data_max, data_max_out)\
    \ is never hit by any directed test. All directed sequences that exercise boundary\
    \ values (TC010 BoundaryRoundtripSeq, FifoCornerTest) write max_data values and\
    \ read them back on separate non-overlapping phases, so din=max_data and dout=max_data\
    \ never coincide on the same clock edge. The cross bin IS reachable \u2014 FifoRandomizedTest\
    \ hits it 3 times \u2014 confirming the condition is valid but no directed stimulus\
    \ targets it.\n"
  consequence: 'The fifo_data_cg boundary_data_concurrent cross reports 75% in directed
    tests (3 of 4 bins hit). The single uncovered bin represents a legitimate concurrent-bus-extreme
    scenario that should be exercised by a targeted directed sequence rather than
    relying solely on randomized traffic. If the randomized seed changes or the test
    is removed, this cross bin would revert to 0% on the (data_max, data_max_out)
    bin.

    '
candidate_interventions:
- 'Add a new directed sequence BoundaryConcurrentSeq to sequences.py that writes max_data,
  reads it back (so dout transitions to max_data), then writes max_data again on the
  next active cycle so din=max_data and dout=max_data are sampled simultaneously.
  Register in CORNER_SEQUENCES for automatic inclusion in FifoCornerTest.

  '
- 'Modify BoundaryRoundtripSeq (TC010) to include a phase where max_data is written
  immediately after a read that pops max_data, creating the concurrent condition.
  (Rejected: modifies an existing plan-mapped sequence, increasing regression risk.)

  '
- 'Accept that only FifoRandomizedTest covers this cross and document the dependency.
  (Rejected: leaves a directed-test coverage hole that weakens regression robustness.)

  '
selected_intervention:
  type: new_directed_boundary_concurrent_sequence
  expected_effect:
  - 'Adds BoundaryConcurrentSeq to sequences.py: fills FIFO with max_data, reads one
    entry (dout transitions to max_data), then writes max_data again on the next active
    cycle so din=max_data and dout=max_data are sampled simultaneously, hitting the
    (data_max, data_max_out) cross bin.

    '
  - 'The sequence is registered in CORNER_SEQUENCES and automatically exercised by
    FifoCornerTest, improving directed-test coverage from 75% to 100% on the boundary_data_concurrent
    cross.

    '
  - 'The sequence scales with DATA_WIDTH (uses self.max_data) and DEPTH (requires
    at least 1 entry), so it remains valid under future parameter-sweep configurations.

    '
  - 'No existing code is modified; the intervention is purely additive (new sequence
    class + one entry in CORNER_SEQUENCES).

    '
regression_risks:
- 'LOW: The new sequence is additive (new class + one list entry) and follows the
  exact pattern of all existing corner-case sequences. No existing test logic is modified.

  '
- 'LOW: The sequence uses self.max_data from ConfigDB, which is already proven correct
  across all existing boundary tests.

  '
- 'LOW: FifoCornerTest runs CORNER_SEQUENCES sequentially with drain cycles between
  them; adding one more sequence extends run time by approximately 10-15 cycles, well
  within the watchdog budget.

  '
validation:
- 'After implementation, run FifoCornerTest and verify the boundary_data_concurrent
  cross shows 4/4 bins hit (100%) in the per-test coverage YAML.

  '
- 'Run all 13 existing tests to confirm zero regressions (all pass, 0 mismatches).

  '
- Verify the new sequence passes its inline checks (dout values match max_data after
  each read).

